    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6666" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακᾰλύπτω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκ-</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>uncover,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				4.952.62
			</span></i> (Epid.); <i>reveal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				85.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά,</span> i. e. his character,
				<i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				20
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. λόγους</span>
			<i>use open</i> speech, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1146
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κάρα</span>”
				<i>unveil oneself, Or.</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					294
				</span></i>
			: so in 
				Med.
			, <i>unveil oneself,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.4.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>remove a covering,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλεφάρων μὴ ἀνακαλυφθέντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Sens.</u>
					444b25
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
				3.14
			</span></i>.</div>
